econdary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lend a hand ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to help", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It feels great to lend a helping hand. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to do some volunteer work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "underprivileged", "type": "name"}, {"content": "lacking resources; poor", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've already spoken with a few of the underprivileged folks that we will be serving.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to fall on hard times", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to lose money or to go through a difficult period", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For the most part they're wonderful people who have fallen on hard times. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "handbook", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small book that contains advice, information or rules", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should have read your volunteering handbook.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "leaflet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a piece of paper that gives you information about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I got a few leaflets in the mail.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "junk mail ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "advertisements for products that are sent to people without being requested", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I thought it was junk mail, so I threw it out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "duty", "type": "name"}, {"content": " responsibility; task", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why don't you start with that while I get the team leader to make a list of duties for us?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Causative Verb: To Get", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " The verb <span class=\"italic\">to get </span>has a couple of different meanings in English. It also has a causative meaning.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Let's review the uses of the verb<span class=\"italic\"> to get</span>:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "1. To talk about things you receive or end up having or holding.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "&nbsp; <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got </span>the impression he wasn't happy. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "2. To talk about things you achieve or obtain.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got </span>a prize for having the best costume.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "3. To talk about a disease or ailment you contracted", "type": "text"}, {"content": "&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got </span>a cold after walking in the snow.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "4. To talk about entering or reaching a place.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">got </span>to the station a half hour late.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use<span class=\"italic\"> get</span> as a causative verb to talk about an action that a person did for you. The subject of the sentence caused the action to happen, but didn't do it directly. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I'm so glad Candice <span class=\"strong\">got</span> you to do this with me!</span><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Get + object + past participle (get something done)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">got</span> my police check sent directly to them.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes, you use <span class=\"italic\">get </span>when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'll get a senior volunteer to store my purse in one of the lockers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Why don't you start with that while I get the team leader to make a list of duties for us?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing Necessity: Should/Ought to/Shall", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the modals <span class=\"italic\">should</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ought to </span>and <span class=\"italic\">shall</span> to talk about necessity in the present, past and future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Should, ought to + infinitive </span> and<span class=\"strong\"> shall </span>express obligation and duty. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use<span class=\"italic\"> should </span>when you offer a subjective opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I think he <span class=\"strong\">should apologize</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">ought to </span>to refer to a more general and more objective opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> We <span class=\"strong\">ought to protect</span> endangered species.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you want to refer to past obligations and necessities, you add the modal <span class=\"italic\">have </span>to the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">should have seen </span>a doctor.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">ought to have been </span>more careful.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">shall </span>to express formal rules and regulations or commands: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Backstage workers <span class=\"strong\">shall </span>wear their credentials at all times.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">They <span class=\"strong\">shall </span>not be allowed to enter.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "New volunteers shall be accompanied by a senior volunteer at all times.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I really should have read it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Absolutely, and we probably ought to scrub the countertops, right?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of a place in your community where there is a need (i.e. homelessness, after-school education).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Brainstorm ten ways in which you could help.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Convert your notes into a one-paragraph proposal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your proposal with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm volunteering ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a proposal about volunteering.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my ideas with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}